      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "As far as I can see `raw.githubusercontent.com` links come from people just trying to link to raw GitHub repository files directly. And it is clear that a bunch of VRChat world creators are using that method by accident.\n\nMaybe some tutorial on how to use [GitHub Gist](https://gist.github.com/) (using [this fix](https://stackoverflow.com/q/46073096/5815327)), so people can learn how to use the `gist.githubusercontent.com` links. And a link to [GitHub pages](https://pages.github.com/) so users can learn about that.\n\nRather `raw.githubusercontent.com` should be whitelisted, I am not sure. Aside from some mention of bandwidth limiting I can't see any mentions of it not being allowed. Maybe VRChat should contact GitHub/Microsoft directly and ask them if it is ok for them to whitelist it, since it will encourage the use of that method.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
